Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UWP Store: older GDK packages (NTFS drive) and the 2019 GDK's XPackage

Applies after 90-uwpstore-minecraft-gdk.patch. GE-Proton already has the EAC runtime support and __wine_unix_call. Found bringing up Gears 5 (2019 GDK, Microsoft Store build):
- appxinstall: GDK packages built before SegmentMetadata.bin store the game as a disk image (GPT with 4096-byte
  sectors, one NTFS volume). xvd_open now falls back to the volume's MFT when the user data has no segment table;
  members become lists of page runs, decrypted per region (resident files are kept in memory). Attribute lists and
  compressed, sparse or encrypted streams are refused rather than guessed at.
- xgameruntime: the 2019 GDK asks for IXPackageImpl as {be3f3e9f-c4b3-424d-9a95-d1af060559a5}; refusing it made
  Gears 5 exit silently right after XGameRuntimeInitialize. Unknown XPackage interfaces are now WARNed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
